--- stdout ---
usage: ask-server [-h] [--port PORT] [--host HOST] [--repos-dir REPOS_DIR]
                  [--repos REPOS] [--api-key API_KEY] [--ask-bin ASK_BIN]

Enterprise ASK server — host agents from multiple repos on one endpoint

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --port PORT           Port to listen on (default: 7232)
  --host HOST           Host to bind (default: 0.0.0.0)
  --repos-dir REPOS_DIR
                        Directory containing repos (each subdir with agents/)
  --repos REPOS         Comma-separated paths to specific repos
  --api-key API_KEY     API key for auth (or set ASK_API_KEY)
  --ask-bin ASK_BIN     Path to ask CLI (default: sibling ./ask or PATH)

Examples:
  ask-server --port 7232 --repos-dir /srv/repos
  ask-server --port 7232 --repos /srv/repos/billing,/srv/repos/auth
  ask-server --port 7232 --repos-dir /srv/repos --api-key SECRET

Then from any machine:
  ASK_SERVER=host:7232 ask billing:architect "What contracts exist?"
        
